# Repo-root prose docs. `pnpm lint`/`pnpm format` run from `www/`, so these were never part of the
# project's formatting scope — but a prettier invocation at the repo root (or an editor's
# format-on-save) picks them up and corrupts them.
#
# The markdown parser reads unescaped `_` pairs in prose as emphasis spans and re-emits them as `*`,
# which silently rewrites identifiers: `aachen_de` -> `aachen*de`, `lcc_step_<strategy>` ->
# `lcc_step*<strategy>`. It also reflows the hand-wrapped ~100-col paragraphs and eats spaces around
# inline code. 6 of the 10 root docs are affected, so ignore the lot rather than escaping prose by
# hand and re-litigating it every time a doc is added.
/*.md
